WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.314 --> 00:00:19.692
When we lose someone
from the neighborhood.

2
00:00:19.775 --> 00:00:21.569
we all feel it.

3
00:00:21.652 --> 00:00:23.195
[Jimmy] What I'd like to know
is who the fuck would

4
00:00:23.279 --> 00:00:24.447
do Pat
in our own backyard?

5
00:00:25.865 --> 00:00:26.824
[Sweeney]
Had a little talk with Danny.

6
00:00:26.907 --> 00:00:28.200
Aw. I appreciate that.

7
00:00:28.284 --> 00:00:29.577
It's a little more complicated.

8
00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:31.746
-[grunts]
-He thinks I gave the order

9
00:00:31.829 --> 00:00:33.372
and you killed Pat Murphy.

10
00:00:33.456 --> 00:00:34.498
If you want to keep him alive.

11
00:00:34.582 --> 00:00:35.791
keep him out
of Hell's Kitchen.

12
00:00:35.875 --> 00:00:38.127
[Polk] You're asking me
to use federal pull

13
00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:39.837
to ship your kid to a safe house

14
00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.214
disguised as a clinic.

15
00:00:42.298 --> 00:00:43.507
[Bridget] I talked to Cahill.
Well. it turns out

16
00:00:43.591 --> 00:00:44.633
he doesn't need the weapon.

17
00:00:44.717 --> 00:00:46.719
I'm sorry. Brendan.
It's gone.

18
00:00:46.802 --> 00:00:48.220
But he does need me.

19
00:00:48.304 --> 00:00:50.389
My target.
Colonel Gerald Markham.

20
00:00:50.473 --> 00:00:51.849
The man who killed
your parents.

21
00:00:51.932 --> 00:00:53.309
This is fucking dangerous.

22
00:00:53.392 --> 00:00:54.852
[Bridget]
And what you do isn't?

23
00:00:54.935 --> 00:00:57.730
I took six kilos from that disco
before we burned it down.

24
00:00:57.813 --> 00:00:59.565
But if we don't deal it.
someone else will.

25
00:00:59.648 --> 00:01:02.067
and they'll just become stronger
and more of a threat to us.

26
00:01:02.151 --> 00:01:03.402
I think it's worth the risk.

27
00:01:03.486 --> 00:01:05.362
We don't deal drugs.

28
00:01:05.446 --> 00:01:06.614
[Mickey] I can't believe
we're back to this

29
00:01:06.697 --> 00:01:08.240
nickel and dime shit.

30
00:01:08.324 --> 00:01:12.244
Your Mr. Sweeney
just donated $100.000!

31
00:01:12.328 --> 00:01:13.579
You think
Sweeney sold our coke?

32
00:01:13.662 --> 00:01:15.247
Fuck yeah. I do.

33
00:01:15.331 --> 00:01:17.500
Eamon Sweeney
with six fucking keys.

34
00:01:17.583 --> 00:01:19.293
-[Sweeney] How much?
-Give you 40 apiece

35
00:01:19.376 --> 00:01:21.669
for the first five.
35 for everything after that.

36
00:01:21.754 --> 00:01:24.590
[Gotti] Eamon Sweeney himself
sold it to Leon?

37
00:01:24.673 --> 00:01:26.592
-That's right.
-So. what's our next move?

38
00:01:26.675 --> 00:01:28.469
[Gotti] Kill that motherfucker
Eamon Sweeney.

39
00:01:30.429 --> 00:01:32.431
I just can't believe
he lied to my fucking face.

40
00:01:32.514 --> 00:01:34.850
Problem is.
you put Sweeney on a pedestal.

41
00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:36.268
We all did.

42
00:01:36.352 --> 00:01:37.770
To Eamon Sweeney.
for always looking out

43
00:01:37.853 --> 00:01:39.647
for the less fortunate.
But now we know

44
00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:41.273
he don't fucking belong there.

45
00:01:41.357 --> 00:01:42.733
He has your loyalty. right?

46
00:01:42.817 --> 00:01:44.734
You would die for that
motherfucker. I know you.

47
00:01:44.819 --> 00:01:47.279
[gunshots]

48
00:01:47.363 --> 00:01:48.864
You think
he'd say the same for you?

49
00:01:49.615 --> 00:01:51.325
Looks like the Italians
weren't too happy with you

50
00:01:51.407 --> 00:01:52.535
selling that coke.

51
00:01:52.618 --> 00:01:53.536
You wanna get a beer?

52
00:01:55.955 --> 00:01:58.582
[sinister music]

53
00:02:27.528 --> 00:02:28.779
[Sweeney]
You know me. Paul.

54
00:02:28.863 --> 00:02:30.239
I wouldn't have asked
for this sit down

55
00:02:30.322 --> 00:02:32.366
if I didn't think
it was in your best interests.

56
00:02:32.449 --> 00:02:33.826
[Gotti]
This guy's threatening war?

57
00:02:33.909 --> 00:02:35.327
I'll send his Irish Mick crew

58
00:02:35.411 --> 00:02:37.746
back to potato land
in a fuckin' box.

59
00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:39.331
[Sweeney] Yeah. those
two hitmen you sent after me

60
00:02:39.415 --> 00:02:41.667
are in fuckin' boxes
right now. John.

61
00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:43.669
Happy to make
the same arrangement for you.

62
00:02:43.752 --> 00:02:45.462
Settle down. both of you.

63
00:02:47.256 --> 00:02:48.673
We're here to talk.

64
00:02:51.635 --> 00:02:53.345
You make a move against Eamon?

65
00:02:53.429 --> 00:02:56.223
Of course not. I don't know
anything about this shit.

66
00:02:56.307 --> 00:02:57.683
He used hitmen
from Scarfa's crew.

67
00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:01.645
Angelo Bruno knows
all about it. Ask him.

68
00:03:01.729 --> 00:03:04.523
Who gives a shit what that mopey
motherfucker Angelo Bruno says?

69
00:03:04.607 --> 00:03:06.317
That guy's a fuckin' liar.

70
00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.610
Angelo's a boss.

71
00:03:08.986 --> 00:03:11.280
I trust bosses.
How about you. Paul?

72
00:03:11.363 --> 00:03:12.615
[chuckles]

73
00:03:14.533 --> 00:03:17.202
This is why I hate drugs. hmm?

74
00:03:17.286 --> 00:03:19.455
Shit like this happens.

75
00:03:19.538 --> 00:03:21.540
You think
Angelo Bruno's a liar?

76
00:03:21.624 --> 00:03:23.959
I'll call him
and tell him you said that.

77
00:03:24.043 --> 00:03:26.211
And if Eamon's story
checks out...

78
00:03:26.962 --> 00:03:28.422
...you and I will have
a problem.

79
00:03:28.505 --> 00:03:30.507
Understand?

80
00:03:30.591 --> 00:03:32.635
Or...

81
00:03:32.718 --> 00:03:34.637
we can agree
to resolve this issue

82
00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:36.639
right here. right now.

83
00:03:38.849 --> 00:03:41.894
Because there's a federal
fucking task force out there

84
00:03:41.977 --> 00:03:44.396
tryin' to put me
in fuckin' jail!

85
00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.815
And they're not
interested in you or you.

86
00:03:46.899 --> 00:03:49.777
So I don't want
dead fuckin' bodies piling up

87
00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.320
that lead back to me!

88
00:03:51.403 --> 00:03:53.322
Which is why
I don't want neither of you

89
00:03:53.405 --> 00:03:54.572
dealing narcotics!

90
00:03:54.657 --> 00:03:56.659
Can you get that
through your fuckin' heads?

91
00:03:56.742 --> 00:03:58.285
Yeah. you think you're talking
to John right now. right?

92
00:03:58.369 --> 00:03:59.745
Because I don't
fuckin' deal drugs.

93
00:03:59.828 --> 00:04:01.580
Fuck yourself. Sweeney.
Neither do I.

94
00:04:01.664 --> 00:04:03.666
I want you two
to make peace.

95
00:04:04.375 --> 00:04:07.252
Whatever your gripes are.
put it behind you.

96
00:04:10.756 --> 00:04:12.800
Eamon Sweeney is
not to be touched.

97
00:04:12.883 --> 00:04:14.718
Or anyone in my crew.

98
00:04:15.469 --> 00:04:16.844
[Paul]
You got that. John?

99
00:04:16.928 --> 00:04:18.764
Not Eamon
nor any of his crew.

100
00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:22.851
I can't hear you. John.

101
00:04:24.937 --> 00:04:25.980
Not to be touched.

102
00:04:27.815 --> 00:04:28.983
Good.

103
00:04:36.115 --> 00:04:37.032
Now shake.

104
00:04:40.077 --> 00:04:41.745
[tense music]

105
00:04:55.134 --> 00:04:58.053
[punk rock theme music]

106
00:05:01.515 --> 00:05:03.976
-♪ It didn't take long ♪
-♪ It didn't take long ♪

107
00:05:04.059 --> 00:05:06.478
-♪ I didn't get far ♪
-♪ I didn't get far ♪

108
00:05:06.562 --> 00:05:09.523
♪ Before the cops were told ♪

109
00:05:09.606 --> 00:05:12.317
-♪ That I'd stolen the car ♪
-♪ Stolen the car ♪

110
00:05:12.401 --> 00:05:15.070
-♪ There was an APB ♪
-♪ APB ♪

111
00:05:15.154 --> 00:05:17.573
-♪ Sent out for me ♪
-♪ Out for me ♪

112
00:05:17.656 --> 00:05:19.825
♪ Ratted out by my own ♪

113
00:05:19.908 --> 00:05:22.786
♪ Now I'm a public enemy ♪

114
00:05:29.168 --> 00:05:31.920
♪ I'm a Catholic school kid ♪

115
00:05:32.004 --> 00:05:34.965
-♪ I'm an altar boy ♪
-♪ Altar boy ♪

116
00:05:35.049 --> 00:05:37.885
♪ I was dropped on my head ♪

117
00:05:37.968 --> 00:05:40.888
-♪ Now I'm here to destroy ♪
-♪ Here to destroy ♪

118
00:05:40.971 --> 00:05:43.724
-♪ I'm a stone-cold killer ♪
-♪ Stone-cold killer ♪

119
00:05:43.807 --> 00:05:46.518
-♪ In the CYO ♪
-♪ CYO ♪

120
00:05:46.602 --> 00:05:49.104
♪ I'm lining them up ♪

121
00:05:49.188 --> 00:05:51.482
♪ And I'm laying them low ♪

122
00:05:52.441 --> 00:05:54.985
♪ But honest as the day
is long that's a fact ♪

123
00:05:55.069 --> 00:05:58.030
♪ I'm not nearly half
as bad as I act ♪

124
00:05:58.113 --> 00:06:01.492
♪ See. I'm always wrong
in the eyes of the law ♪

125
00:06:01.575 --> 00:06:03.911
♪ Parents and priests say
it's the final straw ♪

126
00:06:03.994 --> 00:06:06.872
♪ But sure as the sun.
it rises and sets ♪

127
00:06:19.885 --> 00:06:21.970
This whiskey was casked in '22.

128
00:06:24.848 --> 00:06:26.058
That's before the Depression.

129
00:06:29.186 --> 00:06:30.729
It's almost as old as I am.

130
00:06:30.813 --> 00:06:32.523
[chuckles]

131
00:06:32.606 --> 00:06:34.566
Only 40 cases ever sold.

132
00:06:38.987 --> 00:06:40.739
[coughs]
Oh. Jesus.

133
00:06:40.823 --> 00:06:41.865
That's got quite a kick.

134
00:06:42.991 --> 00:06:45.536
This is liquid bliss.

135
00:06:45.619 --> 00:06:46.912
If you don't mind me saying.
I've had similar reactions

136
00:06:46.995 --> 00:06:48.497
to cough syrup.

137
00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:50.582
[chuckles]

138
00:06:50.666 --> 00:06:52.459
I guess
it's an acquired taste.

139
00:06:53.919 --> 00:06:55.003
So. I take it
the meeting went well.

140
00:06:56.587 --> 00:06:58.132
Gotti got spanked.

141
00:06:58.215 --> 00:07:00.467
No more narcotics.

142
00:07:00.551 --> 00:07:02.469
but...

143
00:07:02.553 --> 00:07:04.138
Big Paul wants me
to basically ignore the fact

144
00:07:04.221 --> 00:07:06.807
that cocksucker sent
two fuckin' hitmen after me.

145
00:07:06.890 --> 00:07:08.517
Do we go after Gotti?

146
00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:12.604
No. I got a better way
to get that motherfucker back.

147
00:07:12.688 --> 00:07:14.940
He's not allowed
to sell drugs. right?

148
00:07:15.023 --> 00:07:17.192
So... we will.

149
00:07:18.318 --> 00:07:19.903
[chuckles]

150
00:07:19.987 --> 00:07:23.532
Okay. Uh. Castellano's
all right with that?

151
00:07:23.615 --> 00:07:24.867
He doesn't have to know.

152
00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:28.745
Look. Jimmy. you were right.

153
00:07:28.829 --> 00:07:30.956
Okay. it makes sense for us
to get into narcotics.

154
00:07:32.166 --> 00:07:33.792
We don't.
somebody else will.

155
00:07:33.876 --> 00:07:36.712
they're gonna get richer
and stronger while we stand pat.

156
00:07:36.795 --> 00:07:38.881
Well. you know I agree.

157
00:07:39.715 --> 00:07:41.925
But I stole that coke
from the Colombians

158
00:07:42.009 --> 00:07:44.803
'cause I happened
to be there.

159
00:07:44.887 --> 00:07:46.471
I mean. we sure as hell
can't go back to them.

160
00:07:47.723 --> 00:07:49.892
I'm gonna
introduce you to Leon.

161
00:07:49.975 --> 00:07:51.852
dude that shylocks for us
up in Harlem.

162
00:07:51.935 --> 00:07:53.020
He can get you supply.

163
00:07:53.103 --> 00:07:55.563
-What about money?
-I'll cover that.

164
00:07:55.647 --> 00:07:58.025
But you gotta do this
on your own. Okay?

165
00:07:58.108 --> 00:08:00.068
I gotta stay on good terms
with Castellano.

166
00:08:00.152 --> 00:08:01.695
Of course.

167
00:08:01.778 --> 00:08:03.864
[Sweeney] And ya gotta
be careful. Jimmy.

168
00:08:03.947 --> 00:08:05.949
This cocaine.

169
00:08:06.033 --> 00:08:07.826
it's a nasty
fuckin' business.

170
00:08:09.077 --> 00:08:10.787
You can't trust anybody.

171
00:08:13.165 --> 00:08:14.082
Slàinte.

172
00:08:15.375 --> 00:08:16.752
Slàinte.

173
00:08:18.921 --> 00:08:20.756
[Polk]
It's hot as a bitch outside.

174
00:08:20.839 --> 00:08:22.966
and the A/C
in this place is for shit.

175
00:08:23.050 --> 00:08:24.593
[Glenn]
Tax dollars at work.

176
00:08:25.969 --> 00:08:27.137
Any word on Danny?

177
00:08:27.221 --> 00:08:28.972
Oh. I hear he's doing fine.

178
00:08:29.056 --> 00:08:30.641
He's only been
disciplined twice.

179
00:08:30.724 --> 00:08:32.016
He hit one of the counselors

180
00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:34.019
and threatened the other one
with cutting her throat.

181
00:08:35.770 --> 00:08:37.939
-I see.
-But let's talk about you!

182
00:08:41.109 --> 00:08:42.861
What about me?

183
00:08:42.945 --> 00:08:45.072
You know. when I invited you
to join this task force.

184
00:08:45.155 --> 00:08:47.699
my superior officers
thought I was crazy.

185
00:08:47.783 --> 00:08:49.660
"He's corrupt." they said.

186
00:08:49.743 --> 00:08:51.870
I said. "So's everybody
at Midtown North."

187
00:08:51.954 --> 00:08:55.540
I said. "You've got to use
a criminal to catch a criminal."

188
00:08:55.624 --> 00:08:58.085
But you. as far as
useful criminals go.

189
00:08:58.168 --> 00:09:00.545
you've been
pretty fuckin' useless!

190
00:09:00.629 --> 00:09:01.880
Does this mean
I'm gettin' fired?

191
00:09:01.964 --> 00:09:05.133
No. it means
you're gonna wear a wire.

192
00:09:05.217 --> 00:09:07.886
What? What.
are you fucking serious?

193
00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:09.263
You tryin' to get me killed?

194
00:09:09.346 --> 00:09:11.556
Get Sweeney on tape
talkin' about something

195
00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:13.725
-we can arrest him for.
-Fuck that. I won't do it.

196
00:09:13.809 --> 00:09:15.811
Then Danny won't get
the help he needs.

197
00:09:16.979 --> 00:09:18.855
I'll have him released.

198
00:09:18.939 --> 00:09:20.899
and he'll be right back
where he started.

199
00:09:22.025 --> 00:09:22.901
You would do that?

200
00:09:24.152 --> 00:09:25.612
Which is it?

201
00:09:30.826 --> 00:09:32.202
-[microphone feedback]
-You got it?

202
00:09:32.286 --> 00:09:33.161
Yeah. Fine.

203
00:09:37.833 --> 00:09:39.167
[Polk]
You got a lotta tattoos there.

204
00:09:39.251 --> 00:09:40.752
Yeah.

205
00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:44.172
Swift. silent. deadly.

206
00:09:45.215 --> 00:09:47.301
Force Recon motto. right?

207
00:09:47.384 --> 00:09:49.052
Yeah.

208
00:09:49.136 --> 00:09:51.346
Legendary.

209
00:09:51.430 --> 00:09:53.056
I'm betting you were
deep in the shit.

210
00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:54.808
You know.
our enemy over there

211
00:09:54.891 --> 00:09:56.226
were a bunch of gooks
I didn't know.

212
00:09:56.310 --> 00:09:57.894
Betraying my friends
is different.

213
00:09:57.978 --> 00:10:00.188
You're working for your country.
same as you were doing then.

214
00:10:00.272 --> 00:10:02.899
Yeah. semantics.

215
00:10:02.983 --> 00:10:05.360
Sweeney's a smart guy.
He won't talk.

216
00:10:05.444 --> 00:10:07.237
It's your job
to make him talk.

217
00:10:07.321 --> 00:10:10.949
This guy is
a serious street guy.

218
00:10:11.033 --> 00:10:12.409
not some dipshit novice.

219
00:10:12.492 --> 00:10:14.870
He can spot the fuckin' heat
in a 40-acre field.

220
00:10:16.371 --> 00:10:17.956
Who's his most trusted man?

221
00:10:19.291 --> 00:10:20.792
It's a toss-up
between Eddie Breen

222
00:10:20.876 --> 00:10:22.377
and Dukey Sullivan.
probably Breen.

223
00:10:22.461 --> 00:10:25.130
Tell him Eddie Breen is one
of our confidential informants

224
00:10:25.213 --> 00:10:26.798
and he's been talkin' to me.

225
00:10:26.882 --> 00:10:28.300
No way he'd buy
Breen would talk.

226
00:10:28.383 --> 00:10:30.677
Maybe yes. maybe no...

227
00:10:30.761 --> 00:10:33.305
so plant that seed with care.

228
00:10:33.388 --> 00:10:35.640
I'm gonna hide the recorder
down your pants.

229
00:10:35.724 --> 00:10:36.725
Be careful
when you're sitting down.

230
00:10:41.063 --> 00:10:42.439
[clicking]

231
00:10:42.522 --> 00:10:44.816
[Brendan]
This is Colonel Markham.

232
00:10:45.567 --> 00:10:49.112
He arrived in Northern Ireland
not long after Bloody Sunday.

233
00:10:49.196 --> 00:10:50.989
They found
this wee sadistic prick

234
00:10:51.073 --> 00:10:52.824
to try and stop our movement.

235
00:10:54.993 --> 00:10:57.329
He implemented
aggressive house searches.

236
00:10:57.412 --> 00:10:59.081
internment without trial.

237
00:10:59.164 --> 00:11:01.249
and shootin'
before asking questions.

238
00:11:02.417 --> 00:11:04.336
Now. as you know...

239
00:11:04.419 --> 00:11:05.962
he was also responsible
for the murder

240
00:11:06.046 --> 00:11:07.422
of Bridget's family...

241
00:11:08.131 --> 00:11:10.926
Tadhg and Maureen McKenna
and those two wee boys...

242
00:11:11.635 --> 00:11:14.304
...all heroes
to the cause in my eyes.

243
00:11:18.266 --> 00:11:19.935
He arrives next month
on the 14th.

244
00:11:20.018 --> 00:11:21.937
and he's being given an award
at the British Consulate.

245
00:11:23.438 --> 00:11:25.148
It's like they're
throwing it in our faces.

246
00:11:25.232 --> 00:11:27.901
The more Irish Catholics
they kill. the bigger the prize.

247
00:11:27.984 --> 00:11:31.029
Aye. They want the world
to think that black is white.

248
00:11:31.113 --> 00:11:33.156
up is down.

249
00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:35.367
Want to rewrite the narrative.

250
00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:37.869
bury British crimes.

251
00:11:37.953 --> 00:11:40.163
And it's up to us.
